.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Lewis and Kasha (1944) showed that phosphorescence comes from a triplet state T_1, whose spin-forbidden return to the singlet ground state makes it far slower than fluorescence. Using realistic rate constants (nanosecond fluorescence, millisecond phosphorescence), jablonski_populations_analytic shows the two emissions separated by six orders of magnitude in time, and phosphorescence_quantum_yield gives the fraction of absorbed photons re-emitted from the triplet.">

